Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.11,0:00:02.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Picture a place where you could nuke the largest
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.41,0:00:04.18,Default,,0,0,0,,city in Greenland
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.18,0:00:06.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Located far in the northern hemisphere with
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.57,0:00:09.49,Default,,0,0,0,,most of its land frozen this place presents
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.49,0:00:11.52,Default,,0,0,0,,an interesting story
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.52,0:00:14.42,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a remote zone with a vast expanse of ice
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.42,0:00:18.09,Default,,0,0,0,,that still exudes an undeniable natural charm
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.09,0:00:20.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Behind the silence and the cold there's a real
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.84,0:00:22.52,Default,,0,0,0,,pulse of life
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.52,0:00:25.82,Default,,0,0,0,,This is Nuuk the largest city in Greenland
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.82,0:00:28.98,Default,,0,0,0,,isolated by eternal ice with a very long winter
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.98,0:00:30.36,Default,,0,0,0,,every year
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.36,0:00:33.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Greenland is the largest island in the world
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.81,0:00:36.56,Default,,0,0,0,,It sits between the Arctic Ocean and the Atlantic
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.56,0:00:39.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Ocean northeast of Canada
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.44,0:00:41.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Most of its territory is covered in ice all
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.98,0:00:43.08,Default,,0,0,0,,year round
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.08,0:00:47.70,Default,,0,0,0,,but this place is inhabited by 56,000 residents
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.70,0:00:50.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Of all the inhabited places Nuuk is the largest
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.95,0:00:51.81,Default,,0,0,0,,city
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.81,0:00:53.98,Default,,0,0,0,,and it accommodates a third of Greenland's
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.98,0:00:55.57,Default,,0,0,0,,population
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.57,0:00:58.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Nuuk is really beautiful and colorful in the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.19,0:00:59.42,Default,,0,0,0,,summer
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.42,0:01:02.42,Default,,0,0,0,,However when winter rolls in the face of the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.42,0:01:05.28,Default,,0,0,0,,city instantly transforms into a white world
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.28,0:01:07.42,Default,,0,0,0,,covered in frozen snow
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.42,0:01:11.11,Default,,0,0,0,,According to history it was founded in 1728
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.11,0:01:13.77,Default,,0,0,0,,by the Norwegian missionary Hans Egede and
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.77,0:01:15.92,Default,,0,0,0,,originally named Godthab
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.92,0:01:17.87,Default,,0,0,0,,which means Good Hope
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.87,0:01:20.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Before Europeans arrived the area around Nuuk
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.71,0:01:23.27,Default,,0,0,0,,had been inhabited by various Inuit groups
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.27,0:01:25.47,Default,,0,0,0,,for thousands of years
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.47,0:01:27.80,Default,,0,0,0,,These Inuit people were hunters and fishermen
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.80,0:01:30.47,Default,,0,0,0,,who relied heavily on natural resources to
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.47,0:01:31.90,Default,,0,0,0,,survive
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.90,0:01:35.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Along the way Nuuk continued to grow and develop
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.93,0:01:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,The city plays an important role in Greenland's
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.38,0:01:41.79,Default,,0,0,0,,history especially after Greenland gained autonomy
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.79,0:01:44.88,Default,,0,0,0,,from Denmark in 1979
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.88,0:01:47.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Nuuk serves as the administrative center for
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.34,0:01:49.53,Default,,0,0,0,,the local government of Greenland
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.53,0:01:52.29,Default,,0,0,0,,making it the capital of the northernmost country
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.29,0:01:53.76,Default,,0,0,0,,in the world
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.76,0:01:59.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Right now Nuuk is inhabited by around 19,872
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.05,0:02:00.49,Default,,0,0,0,,residents
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.49,0:02:03.24,Default,,0,0,0,,They live in houses made with bright vibrant
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.24,0:02:04.61,Default,,0,0,0,,colors
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.61,0:02:07.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Since colonial times greenlandic houses have
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.78,0:02:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,tended to be small and brightly painted
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.00,0:02:14.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Historically each color had a specific meaning
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.15,0:02:17.27,Default,,0,0,0,,that showed what the building was used for
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.27,0:02:20.74,Default,,0,0,0,,A red building symbolized a church or school
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.74,0:02:22.85,Default,,0,0,0,,A yellow building meant the occupant was a
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.85,0:02:24.12,Default,,0,0,0,,doctor
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.12,0:02:26.80,Default,,0,0,0,,A green house indicated that the person living
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.80,0:02:29.77,Default,,0,0,0,,there was a mechanic or worked in the electrical
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.77,0:02:32.59,Default,,0,0,0,,or telecommunications industry
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.59,0:02:35.03,Default,,0,0,0,,A blue house was for employees in the fishing
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.03,0:02:36.04,Default,,0,0,0,,industry
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.04,0:02:39.21,Default,,0,0,0,,while a black building was a police station
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.21,0:02:42.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Until now colorful houses remain a trademark
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.60,0:02:44.03,Default,,0,0,0,,of Greenland
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.03,0:02:47.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Only now residents can choose whatever color
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.03,0:02:50.21,Default,,0,0,0,,they want without having to match their profession
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.21,0:02:52.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Extreme weather is one of the toughest challenges
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.67,0:02:53.81,Default,,0,0,0,,in this city
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.81,0:02:56.80,Default,,0,0,0,,which is famous for its polar climate and long
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.80,0:02:57.98,Default,,0,0,0,,winter
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.98,0:03:00.91,Default,,0,0,0,,For about seven months every year the temperature
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.91,0:03:03.29,Default,,0,0,0,,here drops below freezing
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.29,0:03:05.90,Default,,0,0,0,,March is usually the coldest month
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.90,0:03:08.43,Default,,0,0,0,,which leaves the entire city wrapped in thick
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.43,0:03:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,ice
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.74,0:03:12.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Nuuk goes through a very short summer that
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.03,0:03:14.64,Default,,0,0,0,,lasts only three months
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.64,0:03:17.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Even though it's summer the temperature still
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.04,0:03:21.66,Default,,0,0,0,,feels cold averaging around nine degrees Celsius
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.66,0:03:25.51,Default,,0,0,0,,On December 21st Nuuk experiences the shortest
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.51,0:03:28.59,Default,,0,0,0,,day and longest night of the year
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.59,0:03:31.87,Default,,0,0,0,,On that day the sun doesn't even peek out until
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.87,0:03:33.77,Default,,0,0,0,,11:22 in the morning
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.86,0:03:37.52,Default,,0,0,0,,and sets at 3:28 p.m.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.52,0:03:41.42,Default,,0,0,0,,On the flip side on June 21st Nuuk gets the
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.42,0:03:44.67,Default,,0,0,0,,longest day and shortest night of the year
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.67,0:03:48.23,Default,,0,0,0,,The sun rises at 3:53 a.m.  and only sets at
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.23,0:03:50.85,Default,,0,0,0,,1:00 a.m. meaning you can actually see the
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.85,0:03:53.12,Default,,0,0,0,,sun shining at night
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.12,0:03:56.45,Default,,0,0,0,,As a remote city surrounded by frozen ice it's
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.45,0:03:59.49,Default,,0,0,0,,already got pretty much everything you'd need
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.49,0:04:03.08,Default,,0,0,0,,You can find airports hospitals shopping centers
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.08,0:04:05.78,Default,,0,0,0,,schools and universities
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.78,0:04:09.09,Default,,0,0,0,,In fact the only university in the whole Greenland
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.09,0:04:11.50,Default,,0,0,0,,region is right here in Nuuk
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.50,0:04:14.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Electricity is a big deal for any city
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.46,0:04:16.75,Default,,0,0,0,,and this place is well sorted with its own
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.75,0:04:18.62,Default,,0,0,0,,power systems
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.62,0:04:21.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Nuuk gets its juice from hydroelectric power
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.22,0:04:22.29,Default,,0,0,0,,plants
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.29,0:04:25.22,Default,,0,0,0,,with the main one being the Buksefjord hydroelectric
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.22,0:04:28.88,Default,,0,0,0,,plant sitting about 45 kilometers outside the
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.88,0:04:30.07,Default,,0,0,0,,city
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.07,0:04:32.75,Default,,0,0,0,,It harnesses the natural flow of water coming
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.75,0:04:36.00,Default,,0,0,0,,off the glaciers to generate electricity
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.00,0:04:38.93,Default,,0,0,0,,On top of hydro power they're also pushing
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.93,0:04:42.67,Default,,0,0,0,,for more wind energy to tap into other renewables
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.67,0:04:45.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Getting to Nuuk isn't easy since it's a remote
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.11,0:04:48.17,Default,,0,0,0,,city with zero roads leading into it
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.17,0:04:50.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Planes and ships are your only two options
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.64,0:04:52.02,Default,,0,0,0,,for travel
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.02,0:04:54.59,Default,,0,0,0,,But in the winter ships just aren't reliable
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.59,0:04:56.79,Default,,0,0,0,,because the surrounding waters freeze right
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.79,0:04:57.77,Default,,0,0,0,,up
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.77,0:05:00.32,Default,,0,0,0,,If you really have to go by water you'll need
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.32,0:05:02.93,Default,,0,0,0,,a special icebreaker to carve a path through
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.93,0:05:04.67,Default,,0,0,0,,for other boats
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.67,0:05:07.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Even though it's isolated and deals with long
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.68,0:05:10.96,Default,,0,0,0,,harsh winters Nuuk is blessed with some jaw-dropping
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.96,0:05:12.74,Default,,0,0,0,,natural scenery
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.74,0:05:15.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Just like in other polar regions the night
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.42,0:05:18.89,Default,,0,0,0,,sky often lights up with colorful auroras dancing
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.89,0:05:20.64,Default,,0,0,0,,across the horizon
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.64,0:05:23.03,Default,,0,0,0,,turning the city nights into something truly
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.03,0:05:24.38,Default,,0,0,0,,magical
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.38,0:05:27.21,Default,,0,0,0,,At the end of the day Nuuk is the northernmost
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.21,0:05:30.28,Default,,0,0,0,,capital on Earth and the most populated settlement
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.28,0:05:32.49,Default,,0,0,0,,on the Greenland mainland
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.49,0:05:35.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure most of Greenland is covered in thick
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.33,0:05:38.20,Default,,0,0,0,,ice with extreme weather that lasts forever
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.20,0:05:40.70,Default,,0,0,0,,but life here keeps thriving
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.70,0:05:43.62,Default,,0,0,0,,It's backed by solid infrastructure including
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.62,0:05:46.39,Default,,0,0,0,,a big port and an international airport that
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.39,0:05:49.83,Default,,0,0,0,,keep the economy moving through services fishing
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.83,0:05:51.24,Default,,0,0,0,,and tourism
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.24,0:05:53.93,Default,,0,0,0,,With all that spectacular natural beauty like
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.93,0:05:57.37,Default,,0,0,0,,giant icebergs and deep blue seas Nuuk has
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.37,0:05:59.97,Default,,0,0,0,,become an incredible spot for anyone looking
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.97,0:06:01.69,Default,,0,0,0,,for a real Arctic adventure
